==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission-matrix definition lets Alloy choose any subset of Role x OperationKind as Allowed. The injection then forces at least one cell to be missing, which is exactly what PermissionCompleteness forbids.
    expected to FAIL: PermissionCompleteness
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing the 'exactly one creating op per audit entry' fact allows orphan audit entries (no op created them) or shared ones (two ops point at the same entry). The injection forces an orphan, which directly falsifies AppendOnly's 'one op | op.op_audit = a' clause.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly, FR_018_AuditRetention
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditRetention: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEntryPerSuccessfulSave  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditEntryPerSuccessfulSave.als
    rationale: This fact is what guarantees every successful create/patch/delete writes an audit entry. The injection forces a successful CreateTaskOp that has no associated audit entry, which is exactly the missing-audit case SC-007 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerSave
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerSave: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Without this fact, a successful operation may target a task whose team differs from the caller's X-Team-Id. The injection forces exactly such a cross-tenant success, which violates FR-014 / SC-004 byte-equivalent 404 invariant.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_CrossTeamIsolation
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerOrAdminForMutation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnerOrAdminForMutation.als
    rationale: This fact gates patch/delete success on owner-or-admin. Removing it lets a non-owner non-admin member's PATCH succeed; the injection forces precisely that case (caller != owner AND no admin membership in the team), which the SC-005 invariant forbids.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_008_010_OwnerOrAdminEdit
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_010_OwnerOrAdminEdit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: This fact pins each audit entry's actor and ae_task to the producing operation's caller and target. Without it, audit entries can be misattributed; the injection produces an entry whose actor is not the caller of the producing op, which AttributionCorrectness must reject.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

